===== [-Dapp Wallet, DEXes,-] {+Margin Trading 6.1. Introduction . Margin trading allows eligible Users to borrow Digital Assets and/or fiat currency from Coinbase Credit, Inc. (“ Coinbase Credit ”), an affiliate of Coinbase, Inc. (“ Coinbase ”), in order to trade Digital Assets and/or fiat currency through the Coinbase Site. Coinbase Credit is the lender with respect to all extensions of Digital Assets and/or fiat currency provided to you for the purpose of conducting margin transactions under this Margin Trading Appendix (each such extension, a “ Margin Extension ”). Coinbase acts for itself+} and [-Decentralized Applications 1. Dapp-] {+as agent on behalf of Coinbase Credit in providing the Margin Trading Services described below. References to “we,” “us,” or “our” in this Margin Trading Appendix include Coinbase Credit, except where the context requires otherwise. By enabling margin trading on your Coinbase Account (a “ Margin Enabled Account ”), you agree to the terms of this Margin Trading Appendix and acknowledge that you are entering into a lending relationship with Coinbase Credit. Capitalized terms used but not defined in this Margin Trading Appendix have the meanings given to them in the User Agreement. If there is a conflict between this Margin Trading Appendix and the User Agreement on a margin-related topic, this Margin Trading Appendix controls. 6.2. Eligibility. The services provided by Coinbase and Coinbase Credit in connection with Margin Extensions and Margin Transactions (the “ Margin Trading Services ”) described in this Margin Trading Appendix are available only to Users who satisfy the eligibility requirements established by Coinbase and Coinbase Credit from time to time, as communicated through the Coinbase Site. The Margin Trading Services may not be available in all states or jurisdictions, and Coinbase and Coinbase Credit reserve the right to limit or restrict availability based on applicable state lending, licensing, or other regulatory requirements. Among other requirements, by enabling a Margin Enabled Account, you represent and warrant (and such representation and warranty shall be deemed repeated each time you initiate a Margin Transaction or receive a Margin Extension) that: a. You are, and will at all times remain, an “eligible contract participant” as defined in Section 1a(18) of the Commodity Exchange Act (an “ Eligible Contract Participant ”). For an individual, this generally means you have more than $10 million in assets invested on a discretionary basis. b. The information you have provided to Coinbase for purposes of verifying your Eligible Contract Participant status and other financial information is true and correct in all material respects. c. You will maintain your Eligible Contract Participant status for as long as you use the Margin Trading Services. If you no longer qualify as an Eligible Contract Participant, you will notify Coinbase promptly. You understand that if you cease to be an Eligible Contract Participant, Coinbase Credit will not extend new Margin Extensions to you and your access to the Margin Trading Services may be suspended. d. Your use of the Margin Trading Services shall be for commercial, business purposes only, and shall not include any personal, family, or household purposes. If you are not, or cease to be, eligible to receive Margin Extensions, each of your then-existing Margin Extensions will become due and must be repaid as set forth below. 6.3. Margin Disclosure Statement This Section provides important information about the risks of trading Digital Assets on margin. You should carefully review this Margin Disclosure Statement before enabling a Margin Enabled Account or conducting any Margin Transactions. MARGIN TRADING INVOLVES A HIGH DEGREE OF RISK AND IS NOT APPROPRIATE FOR EVERY USER. YOU SHOULD NOT ENABLE A MARGIN ENABLED ACCOUNT OR CONDUCT ANY MARGIN TRANSACTIONS UNLESS YOU FULLY UNDERSTAND THE RISKS DESCRIBED IN THIS SECTION 6.3 AND CAN BEAR THE LOSS OF ALL ASSETS YOU DEPOSIT (AND MORE). You can see the eligible Collateral Assets, applicable margin parameters, and any applicable Maintenance Margin Requirements for your Margin Enabled Account on the Coinbase Site. The risks of margin trading include, but are not limited to, the following: a. You can lose all of your Collateral Assets, and you may lose more than you deposit. Losses from margin trading can substantially exceed the value of your Collateral Assets and the assets credited to your Digital Asset Wallet and USD+} Wallet. You {+should evaluate your financial objectives, resources, and risk tolerance to determine whether Margin Extensions are appropriate for you. b. The prices of Digital Assets are highly volatile, and Digital Asset markets operate continuously, 24 hours a day, 7 days a week. A decline in the value of assets traded on margin may require you to deposit additional assets on short or no notice. Margin calls and liquidations may occur at any time, including outside of normal business hours. c. Margin trading involves the use of leverage. Depending on the amount of leverage you obtain, a relatively small movement in the market price of a Digital Asset can have a proportionately larger impact on the Collateral Assets you have deposited or may be required to deposit, which can work against you as well as for you. Margin trading also increases your buying power, allowing you to acquire or maintain a greater position in Digital Assets than you otherwise could, and correspondingly increases your exposure to market volatility — a declining market could result in even greater losses. A decline in the value of Digital Assets you purchase or hold on margin can require you to deposit additional Collateral Assets with us in order to avoid the forced sale or liquidation of those Digital Assets, your other Collateral Assets, or other assets credited to your Digital Asset Wallet and USD Wallet. d. You are not entitled to choose which assets are liquidated to meet a margin call or margin deficiency. If we exercise our liquidation rights under this Margin Trading Appendix, we have sole discretion to determine which Collateral Assets and/or other assets credited to your Digital Asset Wallet and USD Wallet will be sold or liquidated, and in what order and amount. You have no right to direct, select, or object to the particular assets that are sold or liquidated, the timing of any such sale or liquidation, the venue or counterparty for any such sale or liquidation, or the price at which such sale or liquidation occurs. e. WE MAY SELL OR LIQUIDATE YOUR COLLATERAL ASSETS OR ASSETS CREDITED TO YOUR DIGITAL ASSET WALLET AND USD WALLET WITHOUT PRIOR NOTICE TO YOU AND WITHOUT CONTACTING YOU FIRST. If the value of your Collateral Assets, after applicable haircuts, falls below the Maintenance Margin Requirement, we are authorized to sell or liquidate your Collateral Assets and other assets credited to your Digital Asset Wallet and USD Wallet to cover the margin deficiency. You are responsible for any remaining shortfall after such a sale or liquidation. Even if we have contacted you and provided a specific date by which you must meet a margin call, we retain the right to sell or liquidate assets at any time without waiting for that date. f. We may increase Maintenance Margin Requirements at any time without advance notice to you. An increase in the Maintenance Margin Requirement may result in the issuance of a margin call, and your failure to satisfy the call may cause us to sell or liquidate your Collateral Assets or assets credited to your Digital Asset Wallet and USD Wallet. g. You have no right to an extension of time to meet a margin call. While we may, in our sole discretion, grant additional time to meet margin requirements, any such accommodation does not obligate us to provide similar accommodations in the future, and we retain the right to sell or liquidate your Collateral Assets or assets credited to your Digital Asset Wallet and USD Wallet at any time without further notice. h. Coinbase Credit may sell, pledge, rehypothecate, assign, invest, commingle, or otherwise use your Collateral Assets and Received Assets while a Margin Extension is outstanding, up to the Reuse Limit set forth in Section 6.7. As a result, your Collateral Assets and Received Assets may not be held in your Margin Enabled Account at all times during the term of a Margin Extension and may be commingled with the assets of Coinbase Credit or third parties. You retain the right to receive Forks, Airdrops, and other distributions on Reused Assets as set forth in Section 6.7(b). In addition, you acknowledge that Reused Assets may not be afforded the same protections in the event of Coinbase Credit’s bankruptcy or insolvency as Digital Assets that remain in your Margin Enabled Account. During any period when your Collateral Assets or Received Assets are Reused Assets, your claim for the return of such Reused Assets may be a general unsecured claim against Coinbase Credit (as applicable) rather than a property right or security entitlement against Coinbase, and you may not recover the full value or in-kind amount of such Reused Assets. 6.4. Acknowledgment and Assumption of Risks You understand, acknowledge, and agree that: a. By enabling a Margin Enabled Account, initiating any Margin Transaction, or receiving any Margin Extension, you confirm that you have read and understood this Margin Trading Appendix in its entirety (including the Margin Disclosure Statement), that you are sophisticated and fully familiar with the risks involved in margin trading (including the risk of loss substantially exceeding your Collateral Assets and assets credited to your Digital Asset Wallet and USD Wallet), and that you have independently determined that trading Digital Assets using margin is appropriate for you in light of your financial situation and objectives; b. You acknowledge and agree that the use of leverage in connection with Margin Transactions magnifies both potential gains and potential losses, and that you have no right to select or direct which Collateral Assets or other assets credited to your Digital Asset Wallet and USD Wallet are sold or liquidated by us in connection with a margin call, margin deficiency, or the exercise of our rights hereunder. c. You are solely responsible for, and voluntarily assume, all risks associated with Margin Enabled Accounts, Margin Transactions, and Margin Extensions, including the risks described in this Margin Trading Appendix and any other risks not specifically identified in this Margin Trading Appendix; d. Neither Coinbase nor Coinbase Credit shall have any responsibility or liability for any loss or damage you incur, directly or indirectly, arising from or related to your Margin Enabled Account, Margin Transactions, or Margin Extensions, and you have not relied on Coinbase or Coinbase Credit for any investment, tax, or accounting advice in connection with your decision to use margin; e. You specifically acknowledge and consent to Coinbase Credit’s right to sell, pledge, rehypothecate, assign, invest, commingle, or otherwise use your Collateral Assets and Received Assets as set forth in Section 6.7 (Right to Reuse Collateral), including that your Collateral Assets and Received Assets may not be held in your Margin Enabled Account at all times during the term of a Margin Extension and may be commingled with the assets of Coinbase Credit or third parties; f. You are acting for your own account and not on behalf of any undisclosed third party; g. Your use of the Margin Trading services shall be for commercial, business purposes only, and shall not include any personal, family, or household purposes; h. Your use of the Margin Trading Services is not prohibited by law or other authority in your jurisdiction of residence; i. You have, or will have at the time of any required delivery, the right to pledge and deliver any Collateral Assets, Received Assets, and other amounts required hereunder, free and clear of all liens and encumbrances other than those arising under this Margin Trading Appendix; j. You specifically acknowledge the bankruptcy and insolvency risks with respect to Reused Assets as described in Section 6.3(h), including that your claim for the return of Reused Assets in the event of Coinbase Credit’s bankruptcy or insolvency may be a general unsecured claim rather than a property right or security entitlement against Coinbase; and k. This Margin Trading Appendix and the Margin Extensions will be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of California, excluding its conflicts of laws principles, except to the extent such state law is preempted by federal law. 6.5. Margin Extensions and Transactions a. Margin Extensions . Subject to the terms of this Margin Trading Appendix, Coinbase Credit may provide to you a Margin Extension to make Margin Transactions. You must meet or exceed any minimum balance and eligibility requirements imposed by us for your Margin Enabled Account to qualify for a Margin Extension. Neither Coinbase nor Coinbase Credit is under any obligation to make any Margin Extension to you, and Coinbase Credit may decline a request to initiate a Margin Extension in its sole discretion. b. How Margin Transactions Work . A Margin Transaction occurs when you use a Margin Extension to trade Digital Assets through your Margin Enabled Account. To effectuate a Margin Transaction, Coinbase Credit lends you fiat currency or Digital Assets, which you may then use to purchase or sell Digital Assets on the Coinbase Site (each such trade, a “ Margin Transaction ”). Upon execution of a Margin Transaction, Coinbase records your ownership of the fiat currency or Digital Assets acquired by you (the “ Received Assets ”) on its internal books and records. c. Open-Ended Duration . There are no term limits on Margin Extensions, meaning that you+} may elect to [-use-] {+maintain open positions on margin for an unlimited duration, so long as you continue to meet your obligations under this Margin Trading Appendix (including the Maintenance Margin Requirement) and subject to+} our [-dapp wallet (“ Dapp Wallet-] {+rights under the User Agreement and this Margin Trading Appendix. d. Loan Ledger . Coinbase will maintain a ledger reflecting your outstanding Margin Extensions and the material terms thereof, accessible to you through the Coinbase Site (the “ Loan Ledger+} ”). [-Our Dapp Wallet allows-] {+The Loan Ledger shall be binding and conclusive evidence of the terms specified therein, absent manifest error. e. Termination of Margin Extensions . Coinbase Credit may terminate any Margin Extension at any time following the second day after such Margin Extension is entered into upon notice to you (which may be oral, in writing, or through the Coinbase Site) and may require+} you to [-access-] {+repay the Margin Extension on the same day. Upon any such termination, the Margin Extension is repayable, together with accrued Margin Fees, in the same Digital Asset or fiat currency in which it was extended. f. Custody of Received Assets . All Received Assets are assets held by Coinbase for your benefit, subject to the terms of the User Agreement (including this Margin Trading Appendix), and the Margin Enabled Account forms part of the Digital Asset Wallet and is subject to the same terms applicable thereto in the User Agreement (including Section 2.7.2 therein), except to the extent of any inconsistency herein. 6.6. Collateral and Security Interest a. Collateral Assets . You agree to maintain+} a [-digital asset browser-] {+specified minimum amount of Collateral Assets that have been approved by us to qualify as eligible for collateral value hereunder. For purposes of this Margin Trading Appendix, “ Collateral Assets ” means the Digital Assets+} and [-link-] {+fiat currency credited+} to [-decentralized-] {+your Margin Enabled Account and all Received Assets, in each case that have not been withdrawn by you, including any assets that are subject to reuse and rehypothecation. For purposes of such calculation, certain Digital Assets may only be valued as collateral on a discounted basis. Eligible Collateral Assets and any applicable valuation discounts (“ haircuts ”) will be determined by us and communicated through the Coinbase Site. b. Valuation . For purposes of calculating your compliance with the Maintenance Margin Requirement, we will calculate (subject to any applicable discounts) the market value of Collateral Assets on a continuous basis. Valuation of Digital Assets will be based on the prevailing value of each Digital Asset on one or more Digital Asset+} exchanges [-(“ DEXs ”)-] {+or trading venues, including those operated by Coinbase or its affiliates. We have discretion to select sources for calculating this market value that we, in our reasonable judgment, believe offer a reasonable valuation. c. Grant of Security Interest . You represent and warrant that the Pledged Assets are free and clear of all liens and encumbrances other than those arising under this Margin Trading Appendix, and that you have the right to grant a first priority security interest hereunder. To secure all Margin Extensions, Margin Fees, and any other amounts or obligations owed by you to us hereunder (collectively, the “ Secured Obligations ”), you hereby grant to Coinbase Credit (and to Coinbase, as agent for Coinbase Credit) a continuing first priority security interest in, lien on and right of setoff against all of your right, title and interest, whether now owned or existing or hereafter acquired or arising, to: i. all Collateral Assets; ii. all assets credited to your Digital Asset Wallet and USD Wallet; iii. any cash, securities, commodity contracts, general intangibles+} and other [-decentralized applications (together, “ Dapp(s) ”). The Dapp Wallet enables users to (i) store Digital Assets; (ii) access a digital asset browser and link to Dapps; (iii) view addresses and information that are part of Digital Asset networks and broadcast transactions; (iv) participate in retail DEX trades and associated DEX activity, and (iv) additional functionality as we-] {+property which+} may [-add-] from time to [-time. 1.1. Ownership-] {+time be deposited, credited, held or carried in any such account, that is due to you from Coinbase Credit, Coinbase, or their affiliates (collectively, the “ Coinbase Entities ”), or that is delivered to or in the possession or control of any of the Coinbase Entities or any of the Coinbase Entities’ agents+} and [-Control.-] {+all security entitlements with respect to any of the foregoing; iv. your rights to any agreement with a Coinbase Entity or obligations owed to you by a Coinbase Entity; and v. all proceeds of the foregoing (collectively, the “ Pledged Assets ”). d. Grant by User . The security interest granted under this Section 6.6 is granted by you to Coinbase Credit (and to Coinbase, as agent for Coinbase Credit). For the avoidance of doubt, Pledged Assets subject to the security interest granted hereunder may be sold, transferred, applied, or liquidated by Coinbase or Coinbase Credit in accordance with this Margin Trading Appendix. e. Further Assurances .+} You [-own-] {+shall take all action that may be necessary or appropriate and that we may reasonably request to establish or maintain the validity, perfection, enforceability, and priority of the security interest in and lien on the Pledged Assets, including, but not limited to: (i) promptly discharging all liens on the Pledged Assets other than our security interest or any other liens permitted herein; and (ii) executing and delivering financing statements, control agreements, instruments of pledge, notices, and assignments, in each case in form and substance reasonably satisfactory to us, relating to the creation, validity, perfection, maintenance, or continuation of our security interest under the Uniform Commercial Code, as in effect in any jurisdiction, or other applicable law. You hereby authorize us to file against you one or more financing, continuation, or amendment statements pursuant to the Uniform Commercial Code, as in effect in any jurisdiction, or other applicable law, provided that the description of the collateral in any such statement is limited to only the Pledged Assets and related property described in Section 6.6(c). f. Control . You, Coinbase, and Coinbase Credit each acknowledge and agree that Coinbase and Coinbase Credit will hold+} and control {+any Pledged Assets for itself as secured party and also as agent and bailee for Coinbase Credit and Coinbase, respectively, and Coinbase will comply with any entitlement orders or instructions originated by Coinbase Credit with respect to the Pledged Assets without any further consent by you. 6.7. Right to Reuse Collateral a. Reuse Right . You agree that Coinbase Credit shall have the full right to sell, pledge, rehypothecate, assign, invest, use, commingle, or otherwise dispose of, or otherwise use in its business, any Collateral Assets and Received Assets in your Margin Enabled Account (any Collateral Assets so used, “ Reused Assets ”), in an aggregate amount not to exceed 200% of the aggregate value of your outstanding Margin Extensions and Margin Fees (the “ Reuse Limit ”). To the extent the value of Reused Assets at any time exceeds the Reuse Limit, Coinbase Credit shall return+} Digital Assets [-held-] {+of equivalent type and quantity to your Margin Enabled Account within two Business Days after Coinbase calculates the existence of such excess. In furtherance of the foregoing, Coinbase Credit may,+} in {+its discretion, instruct Coinbase to transfer Digital Assets from+} your [-Dapp Wallet. As-] {+Margin Enabled Account to accounts of Coinbase Credit or as otherwise instructed by Coinbase Credit. b. Your Entitlement to Distributions on Reused Assets . You shall be entitled to receive any Forks, Airdrops, or other distributions (each as defined in Section 6.10) made on or in respect of Reused Assets that are not otherwise received by you, to+} the [-owner-] {+full extent you would have been so entitled if the Reused Assets had not been reused. Any such distribution that you are entitled to receive will be added to your Margin Enabled Account or to the Reused Assets on the date the distribution occurs (or such other date as Coinbase Credit determines in its sole discretion), and will be treated as Collateral Assets subject to the security interest granted under Section 6.6, except that if Coinbase Credit determines, in its sole discretion, that the distribution is+} of {+a materially different form, type, or character such that it cannot reasonably be added to the Collateral Assets, no obligation to transfer the distribution will arise. 6.8. Maintenance Margin Requirements and Liquidation a. Maintenance Margin Requirement . You must maintain Collateral Assets with a value that, after applicable haircuts, meets or exceeds the minimum maintenance margin requirement (the “ Maintenance Margin Requirement ”) as determined by us and communicated through the Coinbase Site. We may change the Maintenance Margin Requirement at any time, with or without notice to you. b. Margin Calls . If the value of your Collateral Assets falls below the Maintenance Margin Requirement, we may issue a margin call requiring you to deposit additional eligible assets into your Margin Enabled Account. However, we are not obligated to issue a margin call before exercising any of our rights under this Section 6.8, including the right to liquidate your Pledged Assets. c. Authorization to Liquidate . You hereby authorize and instruct us, in the event the value of your Collateral Assets falls below the Maintenance Margin Requirement, to, without further notice to you, sell or liquidate Collateral Assets or use such assets to purchase Digital Assets lent to you, in each case in the manner and amount practicable, in our reasonable discretion, to repay outstanding Margin Extensions either in full, or in an amount sufficient, in our reasonable discretion, to restore the value of your Collateral Assets to an amount equal to or exceeding the Maintenance Margin Requirement. d. Liquidation . When we sell or purchase Digital Assets, we may do so at the prevailing market price at the time of liquidation, in our reasonable discretion. We are not obligated to take market action at a time that provides the best price for you, and we may use the same valuation method and process that we otherwise use on the Coinbase Site, or any other reasonable valuation method, to determine the value of any Digital Assets sold, purchased, or applied. You agree that any such sale is at your instruction. e. No Obligation to Contact . We have no obligation to contact you prior to engaging in any market action under this Section 6.8. While we may attempt to notify you of margin calls or liquidation events, we are not required to do so. Any failure or delay by us to make a demand for additional collateral, or any accommodation we may provide, shall not in any way affect our rights or your obligations under this Margin Trading Appendix. f. Loss of Eligibility . If you are not (or are no longer) eligible to receive Margin Extensions, each of your then-existing Margin Extensions will become due and must be terminated immediately upon loss of eligibility. If you do not immediately terminate your Margin Extensions in full, then we reserve the right to, without further notice to you: (i) sell or liquidate your Received Assets and apply the proceeds to the termination of the Margin Extension; and (ii) liquidate such other+} Digital Assets in your [-Dapp Wallet,-] {+Margin Enabled Account, in the manner and amount practicable, in our reasonable discretion, to terminate the Margin Extension in full. g. Withdrawal Restrictions . You may not make, and Coinbase will not follow any instruction or entitlement order from+} you [-shall bear all risk-] {+to make, any withdrawal+} of [-loss-] {+Digital Assets or fiat currency from your Margin Enabled Account if (i) such withdrawal would cause the value+} of [-such Digital Assets.-] {+your Collateral Assets to fall below the Maintenance Margin Requirement or (ii) an Event of Default (as defined in Section 6.12), or any event that with the giving of notice or lapse of time would constitute an Event of Default, has occurred and is continuing.+} Coinbase shall have no liability for {+declining to follow your instructions in any of the circumstances described in this paragraph. 6.9. Terminating Margin Extensions a. How to Terminate . You must repay each Margin Extension with the same type of fiat currency or+} Digital Asset [-fluctuations-] {+that Coinbase Credit provided in extending the applicable Margin Extension. To repay a Margin Extension, you must have as Collateral Assets a sufficient quantity of the applicable Digital Asset+} or [-loss associated with your use-] {+fiat currency to repay such Margin Extension and using such Collateral Assets to repay the Margin Extension must not cause a margin deficit (the “ Repayment Conditions ”). b. Methods+} of [-a Dapp Wallet. At any time, subject to outages, downtime, and other applicable policies,-] {+Termination . If you satisfy the Repayment Conditions,+} you may [-withdraw your Digital Assets by sending it to a different blockchain address. 1.2. Third Party Services and Environments. The Services and Coinbase Site may-] provide [-access to or link to third-party services, such as DEXs, and/or Dapps (“ Third Party Services ”). The Services enable you to access DEXs and/or Dapps via a Dapp browser or-] {+us with notice+} through [-a Dapp Wallet by navigating away from-] the Coinbase Site {+(or such methods as we determine and notify+} to {+you from time to time) of your desire to effect repayment of a Margin Extension. c. Application of Assets and Restrictions . If you provide Coinbase with instructions to repay any Margin Extension and+} the [-Dapp-] {+Repayment Conditions are satisfied, Pledged Assets of the same type as the denomination of your Margin Extension will be applied toward repayment of that Margin Extension, as determined by us. Until the corresponding Margin Extension is satisfied, Collateral Assets may not be transferred+} or [-DEX, by enabling a native frontend software link within the Coinbase Site, or by purchasing assets in the DEX environment-] {+withdrawn from your Margin Enabled Account except as permitted+} through [-a Dapp Wallet. When accessing Third Party Services, you understand that you are at no time transferring your assets to us. We provide access to Third Party Services only as a convenience, do not have control over their content, do not warrant or endorse, and are not responsible for the availability or legitimacy of, the content, products, assets, or services on or accessible from those Third Party Services (including any related websites, resources or links displayed therein). Third-party Services, such as Dapps and DEXs, may provide access to assets which have high risks of illiquidity, devaluation, lockup, or loss. 1.3. Fees. You may incur charges from third parties for use of Third Party Services. For example, you may be charged fees via a DEX or Dapp that you may access via-] the Coinbase Site. [-Third party fees are not charged by-] {+6.10. Airdrops, Forks, and Entitlements a. In the event that the underlying protocol of a Digital Asset that is the subject of an outstanding Margin Extension undergoes a change in operating rules that results in the creation of new or variant Digital Assets (a “ Fork ”), or a distribution of additional tokens to holders of that Digital Asset (an “ Airdrop ”), while such Margin Extension remains outstanding,+} Coinbase [-and are not paid to Coinbase. Any Coinbase Fee charged-] {+Credit+} will be [-designated as such, and presented before you submit your transaction. 1.4. Supported Assets. To view-] {+entitled to all such new, variant, or distributed Digital Assets (“ New Assets ”) attributable to+} the Digital Assets [-currently supported by-] {+that are+} the [-Dapp Wallet, visit https://help.coinbase.com/en/dapps/using-my-dapp-wallet (“ Dapp Supported-] {+subject of the Margin Extension. Unless Coinbase Credit in its discretion elects to treat a New Asset as forming part of the Margin Extension, you must promptly return any such Digital+} Assets [-”). Your Dapp Wallet is intended solely for proper use-] {+to Coinbase Credit. b. Coinbase and Coinbase Credit may, in their sole discretion, determine whether or not to support either branch+} of [-Dapp Supported Assets. Under-] {+a forked protocol or any airdropped Digital Asset, and shall have+} no [-circumstances should you attempt-] {+liability in respect of any unsupported Fork or Airdrop. For the avoidance of doubt, your rights with respect+} to [-use-] {+protocol changes under Section 2.6 of the User Agreement apply only to Digital Assets that are credited to+} your [-Dapp Wallet to store, send, request, or receive any assets other than Dapp Supported Assets. Coinbase assumes no responsibility-] {+Margin Enabled Account. 6.11. Fees Fees and interest charged on and+} in connection with any [-attempt-] {+Margin Extension will be at the applicable rates as determined by Coinbase Credit from time+} to {+time and communicated to you through the Coinbase Site (the “ Margin Fees ”). Margin Fees may be variable and may change without prior notice to you. If the Margin Fees on any Margin Extension exceed the maximum rates permitted under applicable law, the parties agree that the Margin Fees will be reduced automatically to the maximum rates permitted under applicable law. Margin Fees will be deemed included in “fees” as used in the User Agreement, and Section 3.3 (Fees) of the User Agreement will apply in addition to all other requirements set forth herein. 6.12. Events of Default Each of the following constitutes an “ Event of Default ” under this Margin Trading Appendix: a. Failure to Pay or Perform . You fail to (i) satisfy the Maintenance Margin Requirement, (ii) pay any Margin Fees or other amounts when due, or (iii) repay a Margin Extension when required. b. Breach . You fail to perform any other material obligation under this Margin Trading Appendix or User Agreement and, if such failure is capable of remedy, such failure is not remedied within two (2) business days after notice from us. c. Misrepresentation . Any representation or warranty made by you under this Margin Trading Appendix (including the eligibility representations in Section 6.2 and the representations in Section 6.6(c)) proves to have been incorrect or untrue in any material respect when made or deemed repeated. d. Loss of Eligibility . You cease to qualify as an Eligible Contract Participant or otherwise cease to be eligible to receive Margin Extensions under Section 6.2. e. Insolvency . You become insolvent or admit in writing your inability to pay your debts as they become due; a voluntary or involuntary petition is filed by or against you under any bankruptcy, insolvency, or similar law; you make a general assignment for the benefit of creditors; or a receiver, trustee, or similar official is appointed for you or any substantial part of your property. f. Invalidity of Security Interest . We reasonably determine that the security interest granted under Section 6.6 is or may be invalid, unenforceable, unperfected, prejudiced, or otherwise ineffective in whole or in part for any reason. g. Impossibility or Illegality . You are prevented from making any payment or delivery under this Margin Trading Appendix, or it becomes impossible, impracticable, or illegal for you to make any payment or delivery hereunder. Upon the occurrence of any Event of Default, Coinbase Credit may, in its sole and absolute discretion (and in such order as it determines): (i) terminate, liquidate, or accelerate in whole or in part, any Margin Extension and any obligation to pay accrued Margin Fees and discontinue any Margin Trading Services; (ii) buy in or deem itself to have bought in any assets subject to an outstanding Margin Extension; (iii) exercise any or all rights and remedies set forth in this Margin Trading Appendix (including those in Sections 6.8 (Maintenance Margin Requirements and Liquidation) and 6.13 (Discontinuance of Margin Trading Services)); (iv) exercise all rights and remedies of a secured party under the Uniform Commercial Code, as in effect in any jurisdiction, and any other applicable law; (v) retain, collect, liquidate, apply, and set off any or all Pledged Assets or proceeds thereof against any Secured Obligations; and (vi) take any other actions permitted by law or in equity to protect, preserve, or enforce its rights or to reduce the risk of loss or delay. Notwithstanding anything to the contrary in any other agreement, upon the occurrence of an Event of Default, Coinbase and Coinbase Credit shall have the right to net, set off, and otherwise apply (i) any and all obligations owing from a Coinbase Entity to you, including any obligation to return Reused Assets, against (ii) any and all obligations owing from you to a Coinbase Entity, regardless of whether such obligations are matured, unmatured, contingent, or arise under this Margin Trading Appendix. You agree that the Pledged Assets are of a kind or type customarily sold on a recognized market within the meaning of UCC Section 9-610 and 9-611, subject to standard price quotations, and due to their price volatility may decline speedily in value within the meaning of UCC Section 9-611. 6.13. Discontinuance of Margin Trading Services Coinbase and Coinbase Credit reserve the right, at any time and for any reason, to discontinue or suspend the availability of Margin Trading Services. Upon any such discontinuance, all outstanding Margin Extensions will become immediately due. You hereby authorize and instruct us, as of the date we elect and without prior notice to you, to sell or liquidate Collateral Assets and apply the proceeds, or+} use [-your Dapp Wallet with-] {+such assets to purchase+} Digital Assets [-that-] {+lent to you, in each case to satisfy outstanding Margin Extensions. All Secured Obligations, and the rights of Coinbase and Coinbase Credit in connection therewith (including any security interest granted under Section 6.6), will survive any such discontinuance. This Section is in addition to, and does not limit, any rights of Coinbase under Section 6.10 of the User Agreement. 6.14. Tax Treatment Subject to clarification by the U.S. Internal Revenue Service or the U.S. Department of the Treasury, it is intended that, for U.S. federal income tax purposes, the provision and return of Digital Assets pursuant to a Margin Extension will constitute a lending transaction and will not be treated as a taxable sale or disposition within the meaning of Section 1001 of the U.S. Internal Revenue Code of 1986, as amended, and Treasury regulations thereunder. Coinbase does not provide tax advice. You are solely responsible for determining the tax consequences of your Margin Transactions, and you should consult your own tax advisor before using the Margin Trading Services. 6.15. Bankruptcy Code Acknowledgements a. You and+} we [-do not support. You-] acknowledge and agree that [-Coinbase is not liable for any unsupported Digital Asset that is sent to-] {+this Margin Trading Appendix constitutes+} a [-wallet address associated with your Dapp Wallet. Coinbase may-] {+“master netting agreement” as defined+} in [-its sole discretion terminate support for any particular Digital Asset. Services and supported assets may vary by jurisdiction. 2. Digital Asset Transfers 2.1. In General. Your Dapp Wallet enables you to send Dapp Supported Assets to, and request, receive, and store Dapp Supported Assets from, third parties. Your transfer of Dapp Supported Assets between your other Digital Asset wallets (including wallets off the Coinbase Site) and to and from third parties is a “ Dapp Wallet Asset Transfer ”. We recommend customers send a small amount of Dapp Supported Assets as a test before sending a significant amount of Dapp Supported Assets. 2.2. Pending Transactions. Once a Dapp Wallet Asset Transfer is submitted to a Digital Asset network, the transaction will be unconfirmed and remain in a pending state for a period of time sufficient to allow confirmation-] {+Section 102(38A)+} of the [-transaction by the Digital Asset network. A Dapp Wallet Asset Transfer is not complete while it is in a pending state. Pending Dapp Wallet Asset Transfers that are initiated from a Dapp Wallet will reflect a pending transaction status-] {+U.S. Bankruptcy Code (the “Bankruptcy Code”). b. You+} and [-are not available to you for use in the Dapp Wallet or otherwise while the transaction is pending. 2.3. Dapp Wallet Inbound Transfers. When you or a third party sends Digital Assets to a Dapp Wallet from an external wallet (“ Dapp Wallet Inbound Transfers ”), the person initiating the transaction is solely responsible for executing the transaction properly, which includes ensuring that the Digital Asset being sent is a Dapp Supported Asset that conforms to the particular wallet address to which funds are directed, including any required Destination Tag/Memo. By initiating a Dapp Wallet Inbound Transfer, you attest that you are transacting in a Dapp Supported Asset that conforms to the particular wallet address to which funds are directed. Coinbase incurs no obligation whatsoever with regard to unsupported Digital Assets sent to a Dapp Wallet or with regard to Dapp Supported Assets sent to an incompatible Digital Asset wallet address and/or unsupported network or blockchain. All such erroneously transmitted Digital Assets will be lost. Coinbase may from time to time determine types of Digital Assets that will be supported or cease to be supported. You-] {+we+} acknowledge and agree that [-you may be required-] {+each and every obligation+} to [-pay network-] {+transfer cash, Digital Assets,+} or [-miner’s fees-] {+other property under this Margin Trading Appendix or any Margin Extension or Margin Transaction hereunder is a “termination value,” “payment amount,” or “other transfer obligation” as such terms are used+} in [-order for a Dapp Wallet Inbound Transfer transaction to be successful. Insufficient network fees may cause a Dapp Wallet Inbound Transfer to remain in a pending state outside of Coinbase’s control,-] {+Bankruptcy Code Sections 362(b)(6), (17), and (27). c. You+} and we {+acknowledge and agree that each Margin Extension and Margin Transaction hereunder is a “forward contract” and a “swap agreement” on account of being a “commodity forward agreement,” that each Margin Extension and Margin Transaction has a “maturity date” of more than two days after the date the Margin Extension or Margin Transaction is entered into, that each Digital Asset is a “commodity,” and that Coinbase Credit is a “forward contract merchant” and “swap participant” in each case as such terms in quotation marks+} are [-not responsible for delays or loss incurred as a result of an error-] {+used+} in the [-initiation-] {+Bankruptcy Code. d. You and we acknowledge and agree that each and every transfer+} of {+cash, Digital Assets, or other property under or in connection with this Margin Trading Appendix or any Margin Extension or Margin Transaction hereunder is a “margin payment” or “settlement payment” in connection with a forward contract and swap agreement, and by or to or for+} the [-transaction and have no obligation to assist in the remediation of such transactions. 2.4. Dapp Wallet Outbound Transfers. When you send Digital Assets from your Dapp Wallet to an external wallet (“ Dapp Wallet Outbound Transfers ”), such transfers are executed at your instruction. You should verify all transact